| Member | Kind | Signature (as exported) | Description |
|--------|------|------------------------|-------------|
| `ZodMiniIntersection` | **constructor** (exported value) | `new ZodMiniIntersection(def: core.$ZodIntersectionInternals<A,B>)` | Creates a *mini* Zod intersection schema. The constructor is generated by `core.$constructor` and internally calls `core.$ZodIntersection.init` and `ZodMiniType.init`. |
| *(no other members are declared directly in the file)* | – | – | All public methods (e.g. `parse`, `safeParse`, `refine`, …) are inherited from the base type `_ZodMiniType`. Because they are not defined in this file they are **not** listed here – they will be exercised indirectly through the instance created by the constructor. |

> **Note** – The class does **not** declare its own methods; therefore the only thing we can test directly is the constructor behaviour and that the resulting instance correctly inherits the public API of `_ZodMiniType`.

